,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40248894,"data":"## 4. Confound Analysis \u0026 Research Integrity Assessment\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40249097,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40249281,"data":"### 4.1 Gate Status Summary\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40249479,"data":"- **Split protocol:** ✅ PASS (disjoint partitions, balanced classes)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40249682,"data":"- **Generator isolation:** ✅ PASS (zero OOD leakage into train/val)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40249878,"data":"- **ID \u0026 Path leakage:** ✅ PASS (zero sample ID or file path overlap)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40250082,"data":"- **Exact duplicate check:** ✅ PASS (zero cross-split SHA-256 collisions across all 11,000 images)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40250286,"data":"- **Observed format confound:** ⚠️ **CONFIRMED** (Real is 100% JPEG vs Fake is 100% PNG)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40250489,"data":"- **Observed resolution bias:** ⚠️ **CONFIRMED** (Real is variable/non-square vs Fake is fixed square per-generator)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40250695,"data":"- **Confound mitigation:** ❌ **NOT YET PROVEN** (Hypothesis only)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40250893,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40251079,"data":"### 4.2 Critical Technical Risks for Milestone R2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40251274,"data":"1. **Pixel-Grid Compression Traces:**\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40251469,"data":"   - Standard decoding (`PIL.Image.open(...).convert(\"RGB\")`) maps byte streams to RGB pixel values. It does **not** erase the block boundary discontinuities, ringing, or high-frequency quantization artifacts embedded in JPEG pixels.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40251756,"data":"2. **Resampling \u0026 Interpolation Footprints:**\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40252079,"data":"   - Standardizing to 224x224 forces asymmetric spatial transformations across generators: BigGAN (128x128) undergoes bicubic upsampling, whereas Midjourney (1024x1024) undergoes downsampling. These leave characteristic spectral/interpolation footprints that CNNs can easily exploit.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40252446,"data":"3. **NPR Residual Interaction with JPEG:**\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40252643,"data":"   - The Neighboring Pixel Residual transform ($r = x - f_{low}(x)$) isolates high-frequency components. Because JPEG blocking artifacts (8x8 DCT grid edges) are also high-frequency, NPR may amplify rather than suppress compression shortcuts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40252874,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40253056,"data":"### 4.3 Prerequisite for Milestone R2 Seal\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40253522,"data":"- The presence of severe format and resolution shortcuts is confirmed on `yangsangtai/tiny-genimage`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40253764,"data":"- Before claiming generalizability or forensic perception validity in R2, the research team must decide whether to:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40253974,"data":"  (a) Train baseline R2 models as-is to empirically measure susceptibility to these shortcuts; or\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40254181,"data":"  (b) Implement explicit bias-control preprocessing (e.g. JPEG recompression of synthetic images, anti-aliasing filters) with dedicated versioning before sealing the evaluation protocol.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":109.40254408,"data":"\n"}
